      "inputText": "Hello everyone.\n\nLast year, I self-published a book about my attempt to get really good at playing table tennis.\n\nIt did “well” in the sense that it topped some Amazon best-seller lists and remained near the top for the rest of the year. It’s currently still #1 on the USA Amazon Kindle table tennis best-seller list.\n\nBut despite that, sales haven’t been great.\n\nIn the last year, it has sold:\n\nPaperback: 443 copies — £1,665.39 (~$2,200)\nKindle: 429 copies — £1,003.46 (~$1,400)\nAudiobook: 82 copies — £405.57 (~$550)\n\nTo be honest, I thought there would be a lot more demand. I got pretty excited when I saw the best-seller tag, then quickly deflated after checking the sales figures.\n\nTo the more experienced writers here, how does this compare with your experiences?\n\nIf you’re interested in a more detailed breakdown of how the year went, you can check out my post on it.\n",
